# Whitelist approach: exclude everything, then explicitly include only what
# the Docker build needs. Prevents any stray files (data dumps, reports,
# IDE folders, etc.) from bloating the context or breaking the build.

# Exclude everything by default
**

# But include these (the only files needed to build + run the app):
!app/**
!prisma/schema.prisma
!prisma/migrations/**
!public/**
!extensions/**

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json
!vite.config.ts
!react-router.config.ts
!shopify.app.toml
!shopify.app.consignment-app.toml
!shopify.web.toml
!Dockerfile
!fly.toml

# Re-exclude things that might sneak in via nested paths
**/node_modules
**/build
**/.cache
**/.react-router
**/.shopify
**/dist
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
